  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA cold front, and associated band of showers, continues to \ntrack east across the region, and should exit the area by \nsunrise. Stratus is expected behind the front through the\nmorning, though any significant fog should be limited by a NW\nwind behind the front. The stratus should gradually mix out by\nlate morning into early afternoon, with clearing skies then\nexpected. \n\nDry weather is then expected to continue through Tuesday night\nas high pressure moves east across the Upper Ohio Valley region.\nLowering humidity levels are also expected with NW flow. Warm\ndaytime temperatures, and overnight lows in the 50s, are\nexpected through Tuesday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nModel ensembles indicate a broad trough will begin to approach \nfrom the northern Plains/Upper Midwest region Tuesday night into\nWednesday. At the same time, a closed SE CONUS low is progged \nto phase with the trough as it approaches the Upper Ohio Valley\nregion. \n\nIncreasing moisture and lift in southwest flow should return \nscattered shower and thunderstorm chances to the region on \nWednesday. Individual shortwaves moving through the trough \nshould then maintain daily shower and thunderstorm chances \nacross the Upper Ohio Valley region into the weekend. The\npotential for locally heavy rain and strong storms will need to\nbe monitored, though it is too early to determine those\nspecifics at this time.",
